## Done

Before you say a coding task is finished: `flutter analyze lib test --no-fatal-infos` is clean, and the matching tests in `30-done.mdc` are green. Player text matches the game. Art goes through `CustomAssets` or `KenneyAssets` only. If architecture, Ascend, the world path, distribution, or tooling changed, update `AGENTS.md`.

## Phone, words, and git

Phones are about 360–430 px wide. The live look is the Samsung A56
(`a56-playtest`, 360×780). Web is a fallback, not the product. Testers
never get a build before the owner.

A whole screen or floor that changes size, speed, or layout gets a before
and an after on the A56. The owner picks. Small tweaks ship.

Say session (ett sittande), daily (dagens jobb), and run (ett varv). The
live hero is the cutout skeleton.

Talk in plain, short Swedish. In-game text stays English. Do not explain
tools unless they ask how.

When analyze and tests are green, commit locally without asking. Push, PR,
or tag when the batch needs it. Never force-push or skip hooks unless they
say so in that turn. Daily work stays on `main`. Do not stage
`windows/flutter/generated_*` unless plugins changed. Split a giant file
instead of growing `game_logic`, `spatial_combat`, or a fat shell. New HUD
goes under `lib/ui/shell/`. Delete unused code that saves do not need.
Keep JSON fields old saves may still have.

Hand off in at most 5 lines in Swedish: what you chose, why, what changed,
and what to try on a new save. Wait when they should look at the phone, a
whole screen or floor needs a before-and-after, or a lock or missing fact
blocks the next step. Otherwise pick the next batch and continue.
